module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.Quasicoherent.BigSiteColimits.AffineCover
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.Quasicoherent.BigSiteColimits.PresentationLifting
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# A global presentation is generation of a module and of its relations

A global presentation of a sheaf of modules, in the sense of Stacks 03DE(6), exhibits it as the
cokernel of a map between coproducts of copies of the structure sheaf.  This file splits that
single statement into its two halves and recombines them:

* the *generators*: a coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf maps onto the module;
* the *relations*: the kernel of such a map is again covered by a coproduct of copies of the
  structure sheaf.

The recombination is formal.  In the abelian category of sheaves of modules an epimorphism is
the cokernel of its kernel, and precomposing a cokernel with an epimorphism leaves it a
cokernel, so the composite of a covering of the kernel with the kernel inclusion presents the
module.  Nothing about sites or schemes enters.

What this buys is a reduction of the remaining module-theoretic field of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.PresentingCover` — that a quasi-coherent module on the slice site at an
affine object is globally presented there — to *two instances of one statement*: that a
quasi-coherent module on that slice site is generated by its global sections.  The first
instance is applied to the module, the second to the kernel of the resulting covering, which is
again quasi-coherent over an affine base because the members of an fppf covering are flat.  In
particular the vanishing of the first cohomology of a quasi-coherent module on an affine
(Stacks 03DW) is *not* needed here: it is needed for the step from presentations of the source
and target of a morphism to a presentation of its cokernel, which is
`SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation.of_isColimit_cokernelCofork_of_surjective_val_app`, not
for presenting a single module.

## Main definitions

* `SheafOfModules.IsGeneratedBy`: one sheaf of modules is a quotient of a coproduct of copies of
  another.
* `SheafOfModules.IsGeneratedByUnit`: the generators half of a global presentation.
* `SheafOfModules.HasGeneratedRelations`: the relations half.

## Main results

* `SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation.isGeneratedByUnit`: a globally presented module is
  generated by copies of the structure sheaf.
* `SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation.of_isGeneratedByUnit`: the converse given the relations,
  that is, the recombination of the two halves.
* `SheafOfModules.isGeneratedBy_of_epi_sigmaDesc`: generation witnessed by a family of sections
  over a terminal object of the site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.FibredSite.hasGlobalPresentation_over_of_isGeneratedByUnit`: the
  `hasGlobalPresentation_over` field of a presenting cover for the affine objects, from the two
  halves on the slice sites at the affine objects.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.FibredSite.presentingCoverOfAffineOfIsGeneratedByUnit`: the resulting
  presenting cover.

## Implementation notes

`SheafOfModules.HasGeneratedRelations` quantifies over *every* covering of the module by a
coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf and over every kernel of it, presented as a limit
fork rather than as the chosen `CategoryTheory.Limits.kernel`.  This keeps the statement free of
the sheafification instances that the chosen kernel would need, and makes the hypothesis as weak
as the recombination can use.

The abelian structure on sheaves of modules at the universe in which global presentations live
is not assumed: it is produced inside the proof from
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.hasSheafify_addCommGrpCat` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrpCat`, which hold on every
site whose objects and morphisms lie below the universe of sections.

The identification of morphisms out of the universe lift of the structure sheaf with sections
over a terminal object, used by `SheafOfModules.isGeneratedBy_of_epi_sigmaDesc`, is
`SheafOfModules.uliftUnitHomEquiv`.  On the slice site at an object `U` the terminal object is
`CategoryTheory.Over.mk (𝟙 U)`, so that criterion reads: a family of sections over `U` generates.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06WN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06WN)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u v w r m t

namespace SheafOfModules

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{r}}

/-- A sheaf of modules `N` is *generated by* `O` when some coproduct of copies of `O` admits an
epimorphism onto `N`.  The index type of the coproduct is unrestricted inside the universe of
the sections. -/
@[ega "0 5.1.1" "more general"]
def IsGeneratedBy (O N : SheafOfModules.{m} R) : Prop :=
  ∃ (I : Type m) (P : SheafOfModules.{m} R) (ι : ∀ _ : I, O ⟶ P),
    Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk P ι)) ∧ ∃ b : P ⟶ N, Epi b

/-- **The generators half of a global presentation.**  The universe lift of `M` in which global
presentations are taken is a quotient of a coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf.  On a
site with a terminal object this says that `M` is generated by its global sections. -/
def IsGeneratedByUnit (M : SheafOfModules.{m} R) : Prop :=
  IsGeneratedBy (uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, max u v m} (unit R))
    (uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, m, max u v r} M)

/-- **The relations half of a global presentation.**  Whenever a coproduct `P` of copies of the
structure sheaf maps onto the universe lift of `M`, the kernel of that map is itself a quotient
of a coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf.  The kernel is given as a limit fork, so no
sheafification instance is needed to state the condition. -/
def HasGeneratedRelations (M : SheafOfModules.{m} R) : Prop :=
  ∀ (I : Type (max u v r m)) (P : SheafOfModules.{max u v r m} R)
    (ι : ∀ _ : I, uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, max u v m} (unit R) ⟶ P),
    IsColimit (Cofan.mk P ι) →
    ∀ b : P ⟶ uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, m, max u v r} M, Epi b →
    ∀ (Z : SheafOfModules.{max u v r m} R) (k : Z ⟶ P) (hk : k ≫ b = 0),
      IsLimit (KernelFork.ofι k hk) →
        IsGeneratedBy (uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, max u v m} (unit R)) Z

/-- A globally presented sheaf of modules is generated by copies of the structure sheaf: the
presenting cokernel map is the required epimorphism. -/
theorem HasGlobalPresentation.isGeneratedByUnit {M : SheafOfModules.{m} R}
    (h : M.HasGlobalPresentation) : M.IsGeneratedByUnit := by
  obtain ⟨I, F, ι, hF, b, hb⟩ := h.exists_epi_of_isColimit_cofan
  exact ⟨I, F, ι, hF, b, hb⟩

/-- **Generators and relations make a global presentation.**  If the universe lift of `M` is a
quotient of a coproduct `P` of copies of the structure sheaf and the kernel of that quotient map
is itself such a quotient, then `M` has a global presentation: the composite of the covering of
the kernel with the kernel inclusion is a map `Q ⟶ P` of which the original quotient map is the
cokernel, because in an abelian category an epimorphism is the cokernel of its kernel and
precomposition with an epimorphism preserves cokernels. -/
theorem HasGlobalPresentation.of_isGeneratedByUnit {M : SheafOfModules.{m} R}
    (hgen : M.IsGeneratedByUnit) (hrel : M.HasGeneratedRelations) :
    M.HasGlobalPresentation := by
  have h1 : HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max u v r m} :=
    GrothendieckTopology.hasSheafify_addCommGrpCat.{max u v r m, v, u} J
  have h2 : J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max u v r m} :=
    _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrpCat.{max u v r m,
      u, v} J
  obtain ⟨I, P, ι, ⟨hP⟩, b, hb⟩ := hgen
  obtain ⟨K, Q, κ, ⟨hQ⟩, a, ha⟩ :=
    hrel I P ι hP b hb _ (kernel.ι b) (kernel.condition b) (kernelIsKernel b)
  refine ⟨I, K, P, Q, ι, κ, ⟨hP⟩, ⟨hQ⟩, a ≫ kernel.ι b, b, ?_, ⟨?_⟩⟩
  · rw [Category.assoc, kernel.condition b, comp_zero]
  · exact isCokernelEpiComp (Abelian.epiIsCokernelOfKernel _ (kernelIsKernel b)) a rfl

/-- **Generation by a family of sections over a terminal object.**  On a site with a terminal
object `Z`, a family of sections of `N` over `Z` generates `N` as soon as the induced map from
the coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf is an epimorphism; the map induced by a section
is `SheafOfModules.fromUliftUnit`. -/
theorem isGeneratedBy_of_epi_sigmaDesc {I : Type (max t r)}
    {N : SheafOfModules.{max t r} R}
    [HasCoproduct (fun _ : I => uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, t} (unit R))]
    {Z : C} (hZ : IsTerminal Z) (s : I → N.val.obj (op Z))
    (h : Epi (Sigma.desc fun i => fromUliftUnit.{u, v, r, t} hZ (s i))) :
    IsGeneratedBy (uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, t} (unit R)) N :=
  ⟨I, _, Sigma.ι _, ⟨coproductIsCoproduct _⟩, _, h⟩

end SheafOfModules

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.FibredSite

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
  {𝒳 : Type v} [Category.{w} 𝒳] (p : 𝒳 ⥤ BigFppfOver B S hS)

/-- **Quasi-coherent modules are globally presented on the slice site at an affine object**,
given that on those slice sites a quasi-coherent module and the relations between its generators
are both generated by copies of the structure sheaf.  Quasi-coherence passes to the slice by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent_over`, and the two halves recombine by
`SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation.of_isGeneratedByUnit`. -/
theorem hasGlobalPresentation_over_of_isGeneratedByUnit (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    (hgen : ∀ (i : AffineObjects B S hS p)
      (N : SheafOfModules.{u}
        ((ringStructureSheafCore B S hS p hp .fppf).over (affineObj B S hS p i))),
      N.IsQuasicoherentOnSite → N.IsGeneratedByUnit ∧ N.HasGeneratedRelations)
    (M : SheafOfModules.{u} (ringStructureSheafCore B S hS p hp .fppf))
    (hM : M.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) (i : AffineObjects B S hS p) :
    (M.over (affineObj B S hS p i)).HasGlobalPresentation :=
  have h := hgen i _
    (_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent_over M hM (affineObj B S hS p i))
  SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation.of_isGeneratedByUnit h.1 h.2

/-- **The affine objects as a presenting cover, from generation on the affine slice sites.**
This is `AlgebraicGeometry.FibredSite.presentingCoverOfAffine` with its global-presentation
field replaced by the two generation conditions of this file. -/
def presentingCoverOfAffineOfIsGeneratedByUnit (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) (K : Type u)
    [Category.{u} K]
    (hgen : ∀ (i : AffineObjects B S hS p)
      (N : SheafOfModules.{u}
        ((ringStructureSheafCore B S hS p hp .fppf).over (affineObj B S hS p i))),
      N.IsQuasicoherentOnSite → N.IsGeneratedByUnit ∧ N.HasGeneratedRelations)
    (hcolim : ∀ (i : AffineObjects B S hS p)
      (D : K ⥤ SheafOfModules.{u}
        ((ringStructureSheafCore B S hS p hp .fppf).over (affineObj B S hS p i)))
      (c : Cocone D), IsColimit c → (∀ k, (D.obj k).HasGlobalPresentation) →
        c.pt.HasGlobalPresentation) :
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.PresentingCover
      (ringStructureSheafCore B S hS p hp .fppf) K :=
  presentingCoverOfAffine B S hS p hp K
    (fun M hM i => hasGlobalPresentation_over_of_isGeneratedByUnit B S hS p hp hgen M hM i)
    hcolim

end AlgebraicGeometry.FibredSite

end
